.TH HTTP_GET_HEADER 3
.SH NAME
http_get_header \- find a header in the head of a response
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "char* http_get_header(char* " data ", size_t " n ", const char* " name ", size_t* " result_len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_get_header ()
looks for the header
.I name
(ignoring case) in the
.I n
bytes at
.IR data ,
which hold the head of a response as
.I response->data
does. The first line, the status line, is skipped. It returns a pointer to the
value, after the colon and the white space, and stores the length of the value (up to the CR or LF) in
.I *result_len
if that is not 0.
.SH RETURN VALUE
A pointer into data, the value is not terminated; 0 if there is no such header.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
size_t n;
char* type = http_get_header(r->data.s, r->headers_len, "Content-Type", &n);

if(type && byte_finds(type, n, "ndjson") < n)
  ...
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
http_canread(3), http_skip_header(3)
